WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.330
A coffin is carried
into a Catholic church.

2
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:07.040
At the door, the priest
sprinkles it with holy water.

3
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.520
A white cloth is spread over it.

4
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.200
A tall candle burns beside it.

5
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:18.600
Water, a white garment and a lit candle:
the same person met all three at baptism.

6
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.220
So why does a funeral use the same candle,

7
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.170
water and white cloth as a baptism?

8
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.810
In this mission, you'll follow
a funeral in three stages:

9
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.620
home, church and cemetery.

10
00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:33.370
Then you'll see what a
priest brings to the dying,

11
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.760
including Communion called
food for the journey.

12
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:42.270
Your mission: find out why a Catholic
funeral uses the same signs as a baptism.
